@startuml
title Clases Classifier - Modelos de Clasificación

abstract class Classifier {
  # id : str
  # sp : float
  # model_type : str
  # all_classes : List[str]
  + get_sp() : float
  + get_id() : str
  {abstract} + fit(X_train, y_train) : TrainResult
  {abstract} + predict(X_test) : NDArray
  {abstract} + evaluate(X_test, y_test) : EvaluationMetrics
  + save_model(path) : bool
  + load_model(path) : Classifier
}

' ============= MODELOS DEEP LEARNING =============
class CNN {
  - kernels : List[Kernel]
  - pooling : List[Pool]
  - dense_layers : List[DenseLayer]
  - dropout : float
  - epochs : int
  - batch_size : int
  - learning_rate : float
  - optimizer : str
  --
  + fit() : TrainResult
  + predict() : NDArray
  + evaluate() : EvaluationMetrics
}

class LSTM {
  - lstm_layers : List[LSTMLayer]
  - dense_layers : List[DenseLayer]
  - pooling_strategy : str
  - dropout : float
  - epochs : int
  - batch_size : int
  - learning_rate : float
  - optimizer : str
  --
  + fit() : TrainResult
  + predict() : NDArray
  + evaluate() : EvaluationMetrics
}

class GRU {
  - gru_layers : List[GRULayer]
  - dense_layers : List[DenseLayer]
  - pooling_strategy : str
  - dropout : float
  - epochs : int
  - batch_size : int
  - learning_rate : float
  - optimizer : str
  --
  + fit() : TrainResult
  + predict() : NDArray
  + evaluate() : EvaluationMetrics
}

class SVNN {
  - input_layer : int
  - hidden_layers : List[int]
  - output_layer : int
  - activation : str
  - dropout : float
  - epochs : int
  - batch_size : int
  - learning_rate : float
  --
  + fit() : TrainResult
  + predict() : NDArray
  + evaluate() : EvaluationMetrics
}

' ============= MODELOS MACHINE LEARNING =============
class SVM {
  - kernel : str
  - C : float
  - gamma : str
  - degree : int
  - class_weight : str
  --
  + fit() : TrainResult
  + predict() : NDArray
  + evaluate() : EvaluationMetrics
}

class RandomForest {
  - n_estimators : int
  - max_depth : int
  - min_samples_split : int
  - min_samples_leaf : int
  - max_features : str
  - class_weight : str
  --
  + fit() : TrainResult
  + predict() : NDArray
  + evaluate() : EvaluationMetrics
}

' ============= COMPONENTES AUXILIARES =============
class Kernel {
  + weights : NDArray
  + name : str
}

class Pool {
  + type : str
  + size : Tuple[int, int]
  + strides : Tuple[int, int]
}

class DenseLayer {
  + units : int
  + activation : ActivationFunction
}

class LSTMLayer {
  + hidden_size : int
  + bidirectional : bool
  + num_layers : int
  + dropout : float
  + return_sequences : bool
}

class GRULayer {
  + hidden_size : int
  + bidirectional : bool
  + num_layers : int
  + dropout : float
  + return_sequences : bool
}

class TrainResult {
  + train_accuracy : float
  + val_accuracy : float
  + train_loss : float
  + val_loss : float
  + history : dict
}

class EvaluationMetrics {
  + accuracy : float
  + precision : float
  + recall : float
  + f1_score : float
  + confusion_matrix : NDArray
  + roc_auc : float
}

' ============= HERENCIAS =============
Classifier <|-- CNN
Classifier <|-- LSTM
Classifier <|-- GRU
Classifier <|-- SVNN
Classifier <|-- SVM
Classifier <|-- RandomForest

' ============= COMPOSICIONES =============
CNN *-- Kernel
CNN *-- Pool
CNN *-- DenseLayer
LSTM *-- LSTMLayer
LSTM *-- DenseLayer
GRU *-- GRULayer
GRU *-- DenseLayer
SVNN *-- DenseLayer

' ============= RETORNOS =============
Classifier ..> TrainResult : returns
Classifier ..> EvaluationMetrics : returns

note right of Classifier
  **Clase base abstracta para modelos**

  Todos los modelos heredan de Classifier
  y deben implementar:
  - fit(): Entrenar modelo
  - predict(): Inferencia
  - evaluate(): Métricas de evaluación

  Soporta serialización Pydantic
  para guardar configuraciones
end note

note bottom of CNN
  **Convolutional Neural Network**

  Arquitectura flexible con:
  - Kernels personalizados (2D)
  - Pooling (Max/Avg)
  - Capas densas finales
  - Dropout para regularización

  Usa TensorFlow/Keras
end note

note bottom of LSTM
  **Long Short-Term Memory**

  Redes recurrentes con:
  - Múltiples capas LSTM apiladas
  - Opción bidireccional
  - Pooling strategies: last/mean/max/attn
  - Capas densas de salida

  Ideal para series temporales
end note

note bottom of SVM
  **Support Vector Machine**

  Clasificador clásico con:
  - Kernels: linear, rbf, poly, sigmoid
  - Regularización C
  - Gamma configurable

  Usa Scikit-learn
  Eficiente para datasets pequeños
end note

note bottom of RandomForest
  **Random Forest Classifier**

  Ensemble de árboles de decisión:
  - N estimadores configurables
  - Control de profundidad
  - Balance de clases

  Usa Scikit-learn
  Robusto y versátil
end note

@enduml
